# Pairs with NoKeyLost. Breaks H, the property #4522's fix relies on: every
# write acknowledged after a saga's prepare P on the same leaf is stamped above
# P. A later write stamped below P loses to the saga's drain and to the
# committed-values backstop, both last-writer-wins at P. Production's known
# exceptions are a DeleteRange stamped at its issue (#4530) and an idempotent
# retry that reuses its issue stamp. The edit lies in WVal, the operator that
# stamps the later write, so the mutation declares no PERTURBS.
MODULE: NoKeyLostLaterWriteBelowP
TARGET: NoKeyLost
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: a later write stamped below the saga's prepare loses to the drain or the backstop at P

--- FIND
WVal(c, s) == IF KnowsP(c, s) THEN LaterV ELSE LaterLowV
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: the later write is stamped below P even on a leaf that saw P.
WVal(c, s) == LaterLowV
--- END